BIBS_REG(7,{"n":7,"t":"Business Ownership","tb":"ব্যবসার মালিকানা","u":"Units 10–11","slides":57,"pdf":"Unit 10 and 11 - BusinessOwnership.pdf","steps":[{"id":"concept","k":"concept","t":"Big picture","tb":"বড় ছবি","sl":[],"h":"<div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<p>When you start a business you must choose its legal form. The choice decides <b>who owns it, who controls it, who pays tax, and whose house is at risk if the business fails</b>. Study questions: <b>7.1</b> factors in choosing (slides 3–7); <b>7.2</b> sole proprietorship (8–12); <b>7.3</b> partnerships (13–21); <b>7.4</b> corporations C, S, B (22–32); <b>7.5</b> hybrids LLC and LLP (33–40); <b>7.6</b> franchises (41–47); <b>7.7</b> mergers and acquisitions (48–57).</p>\n<p><b>3-minute version:</b> <i>Sole proprietor</i> = one owner, unlimited liability, easy to start. <i>Partnership</i> = 2+ owners share profits and losses; <i>general</i> (equal, unlimited liability) vs <i>limited</i> (limited liability and say). <i>C corp</i> = separate legal entity, limited liability, can sell stock, <b>double taxation</b>. <i>S corp</i> = pass-through tax, no double tax, stricter rules. <i>B corp</i> = for-profit with a public benefit and annual benefit reports. <i>LLC</i> = limited liability + partnership tax flexibility (owners = members). <i>LLP</i> = partners protected from each other's misconduct. <i>Franchise</i> = franchisor licenses brand/methods to franchisee. <i>Merger</i> = two firms become one (horizontal = same industry; vertical = buyer-seller supply chain); <i>acquisition</i> = one buys another's assets.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p>ব্যবসা শুরুর সময় আইনি রূপ বেছে নিতে হয়। এই পছন্দ ঠিক করে <b>মালিক কে, নিয়ন্ত্রণ কার, কর কে দেয়, আর ব্যবসা ব্যর্থ হলে কার ঘরবাড়ি ঝুঁকিতে</b>। স্টাডি প্রশ্ন: <b>৭.১</b> বেছে নেওয়ার বিবেচ্য বিষয় (স্লাইড ৩–৭); <b>৭.২</b> একক মালিকানা (৮–১২); <b>৭.৩</b> অংশীদারি (১৩–২১); <b>৭.৪</b> কর্পোরেশন C, S, B (২২–৩২); <b>৭.৫</b> হাইব্রিড LLC ও LLP (৩৩–৪০); <b>৭.৬</b> ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ (৪১–৪৭); <b>৭.৭</b> একীভূতকরণ ও অধিগ্রহণ (৪৮–৫৭)।</p>\n<p><b>৩ মিনিটের সারাংশ:</b> <i>একক মালিক</i> = একজন মালিক, অসীম দায়, শুরু সহজ। <i>অংশীদারি</i> = ২+ মালিক লাভ-ক্ষতি ভাগ করেন; <i>সাধারণ</i> (সমান, অসীম দায়) বনাম <i>সীমিত</i> (সীমিত দায় ও সীমিত মতামত)। <i>C কর্পোরেশন</i> = আলাদা আইনি সত্তা, সীমিত দায়, শেয়ার বেচতে পারে, <b>দ্বৈত কর</b>। <i>S কর্পোরেশন</i> = পাস-থ্রু কর, দ্বৈত কর নেই, কড়া নিয়ম। <i>B কর্পোরেশন</i> = জনকল্যাণমুখী মুনাফাভিত্তিক, বার্ষিক সুবিধা প্রতিবেদন। <i>LLC</i> = সীমিত দায় + অংশীদারির করের নমনীয়তা (মালিক = সদস্য)। <i>LLP</i> = একজন অংশীদার অন্যের অন্যায় থেকে সুরক্ষিত। <i>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ</i> = ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজর ব্র্যান্ড/পদ্ধতি লাইসেন্স দেন। <i>একীভূতকরণ</i> = দুই প্রতিষ্ঠান এক (অনুভূমিক = একই শিল্প; উল্লম্ব = ক্রেতা-বিক্রেতা সরবরাহ শিকল); <i>অধিগ্রহণ</i> = একটি অন্যের সম্পদ কেনে।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s01","k":"slide","t":"Title and outcomes","tb":"শিরোনাম ও ফলাফল","sl":[1,2],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 1–2 of 57 · স্লাইড ১–২ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 1) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s01.webp\" alt=\"Slide 1 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s02.webp\" alt=\"Slide 2 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Introduction to Business Business Ownership</p><p>Module Learning Outcomes Distinguish among the forms of business ownership 7.1: List and explain the important factors in choosing an organizational type 7.2: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of sole proprietorships 7.3: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of partnerships 7.4: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of corporations 7.5: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of hybrid forms of business ownership 7.6: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of franchises 7.7: Describe the two types of mergers and acquisitions</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> Seven outcomes = study questions <b>7.1–7.7</b> (Units 10 & 11). Prepare <b>one comparison table</b> of all forms: owners, liability, tax, capital, life.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> সাতটি ফলাফল = স্টাডি প্রশ্ন <b>৭.১–৭.৭</b> (ইউনিট ১০ ও ১১)। সব রূপের <b>একটি তুলনা টেবিল</b> তৈরি রাখো: মালিক, দায়, কর, মূলধন, স্থায়িত্ব।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"q7-1","k":"lesson","t":"Study question 7.1 — Factors in choosing an organizational type","tb":"স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.১ — সংগঠনের ধরন বেছে নেওয়ার বিবেচ্য বিষয়","sl":[],"h":"<p class=\"lesson-q\"><b>Study question 7.1</b> · স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.১</p><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<p>Slides 3–7: list and explain the factors.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p>স্লাইড ৩–৭: বিবেচ্য বিষয়ের তালিকা ও ব্যাখ্যা।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s03","k":"slide","t":"Forms and factors","tb":"রূপ ও বিবেচ্য বিষয়","sl":[3,4,5,6],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 3–6 of 57 · স্লাইড ৩–৬ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 3) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s03.webp\" alt=\"Slide 3 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s04.webp\" alt=\"Slide 4 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s05.webp\" alt=\"Slide 5 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s06.webp\" alt=\"Slide 6 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Choosing an Organizational Type</p><p>Learning Outcomes: Choosing an Organizational Type 7.1: List and explain the important factors in choosing an organizational type 7.1.1: List the important factors in choosing an organizational type 7.1.2: Explain the important factors in choosing an organizational type</p><p>Forms of Business Ownership • Business Organizational Options:</p><p>• Sole proprietorship • General partnership • Franchise • Limited partnerships and limited liability partnerships (LLP) • Limited liability company (LLC) • C Corporation • S Corporation</p><p>• Each type of business has its own set of risks and rewards, costs and benefits. • Picking the best type depends on the nature of the business opportunity and the level of personal exposure to risk the owner is willing to accept.</p><p>Considerations in Choosing an Organizational Type • Cost of start up • Control vs. responsibility • Do you want to share the profits? • Taxation • Entrepreneurial ability • Risk tolerance • Financing • Continuity and transferability</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> Options: <b>sole proprietorship, general partnership, franchise, limited partnership/LLP, LLC, C corporation, S corporation</b>. Each has its own <b>risks and rewards, costs and benefits</b>; the best one depends on the <b>business opportunity</b> and the <b>personal risk</b> the owner will accept. <b>Eight factors:</b> (1) <b>cost of start-up</b>, (2) <b>control vs responsibility</b>, (3) <b>sharing profits</b>, (4) <b>taxation</b>, (5) <b>entrepreneurial ability</b>, (6) <b>risk tolerance</b>, (7) <b>financing</b>, (8) <b>continuity and transferability</b>.</p><p class=\"lab lab-K\"><b>Exam tip:</b> Memory: <b>C-C-S-T-E-R-F-C</b>. Practice Q1: full control means <b>full responsibility and liability</b>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> বিকল্প: <b>একক মালিকানা, সাধারণ অংশীদারি, ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ, সীমিত অংশীদারি/LLP, LLC, C কর্পোরেশন, S কর্পোরেশন</b>। প্রতিটির নিজস্ব <b>ঝুঁকি-পুরস্কার, খরচ-সুবিধা</b>; সেরাটি নির্ভর করে <b>ব্যবসার সুযোগ</b> ও মালিকের <b>ব্যক্তিগত ঝুঁকি</b> নেওয়ার ক্ষমতার উপর। <b>আটটি বিষয়:</b> (১) <b>শুরুর খরচ</b>, (২) <b>নিয়ন্ত্রণ বনাম দায়</b>, (৩) <b>লাভ ভাগ</b>, (৪) <b>কর</b>, (৫) <b>উদ্যোক্তা সক্ষমতা</b>, (৬) <b>ঝুঁকি সহনশীলতা</b>, (৭) <b>অর্থায়ন</b>, (৮) <b>ধারাবাহিকতা ও হস্তান্তর</b>।</p><p class=\"lab lab-K\"><b>পরীক্ষার টিপস:</b> মনে রাখো: শুরুর খরচ, নিয়ন্ত্রণ, লাভ ভাগ, কর, উদ্যোক্তা সক্ষমতা, ঝুঁকি, অর্থায়ন, ধারাবাহিকতা। অনুশীলনী ১: পূর্ণ নিয়ন্ত্রণ মানে <b>পূর্ণ দায়</b>।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s07","k":"slide","t":"Practice question 1","tb":"অনুশীলনী প্রশ্ন ১","sl":[7],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slide 7 of 57 · স্লাইড ৭ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 7) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s07.webp\" alt=\"Slide 7 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Practice Question 1 Which of the following is a downside of choosing a business structure where the owner has full control? A. The owner must hire a CPA for the business B. The owner has full responsibility and liability for the business C. The owner must work all hours the business is open D. The owner cannot use their real name when obtaining a business license</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Answer: B</b> — the downside of full control is <b>full responsibility and liability</b> for the business.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>উত্তর: B</b> — পূর্ণ নিয়ন্ত্রণের অসুবিধা ব্যবসার <b>পূর্ণ দায় ও দায়বদ্ধতা</b>।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"c7-1","k":"check","t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","sl":[],"h":"","z":{"t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","items":[{"q":"Which is NOT a factor in choosing an organizational type?","qbn":"সংগঠনের ধরন বেছে নেওয়ার বিবেচ্য বিষয় নয় কোনটি?","ans":3,"opts":["Taxation · কর","Risk tolerance · ঝুঁকি সহনশীলতা","Financing · অর্থায়ন","The owner's favourite colour · মালিকের প্রিয় রং"],"exp":"Factors include start-up cost, control, profit sharing, taxation, ability, risk, financing, continuity.","expbn":"বিবেচ্য বিষয়: শুরুর খরচ, নিয়ন্ত্রণ, লাভ ভাগ, কর, সক্ষমতা, ঝুঁকি, অর্থায়ন, ধারাবাহিকতা।"},{"q":"The downside of having full control of a business is…","qbn":"ব্যবসায় পূর্ণ নিয়ন্ত্রণের অসুবিধা…","ans":1,"opts":["paying no tax · কর না দেওয়া","full responsibility and liability · পূর্ণ দায় ও দায়বদ্ধতা","no profit · মুনাফা না থাকা","needing a CPA · CPA লাগা"],"exp":"Control and responsibility go together.","expbn":"নিয়ন্ত্রণ ও দায় একসাথে যায়।"}]}},{"id":"q7-2","k":"lesson","t":"Study question 7.2 — Sole proprietorships","tb":"স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.২ — একক মালিকানা","sl":[],"h":"<p class=\"lesson-q\"><b>Study question 7.2</b> · স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.২</p><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<p>Slides 8–12.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p>স্লাইড ৮–১২।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s08","k":"slide","t":"Sole proprietorship","tb":"একক মালিকানা","sl":[8,9,10,11],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 8–11 of 57 · স্লাইড ৮–১১ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 8) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s08.webp\" alt=\"Slide 8 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s09.webp\" alt=\"Slide 9 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s10.webp\" alt=\"Slide 10 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s11.webp\" alt=\"Slide 11 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Sole Proprietorship</p><p>Learning Outcomes: Sole proprietorship 7.2: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of sole proprietorships 7.2.1: Define sole proprietorship 7.2.2: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of sole proprietorships</p><p>Defining Sole Proprietorship • Sole proprietorships are:</p><p>• Owned and run by one person • Have no distinction between the business •</p><p>•</p><p>and the owner Businesses where the owner is entitled to all business profits and is responsible for all business debts, losses, and liabilities The simplest and most common legal structure for a business</p><p>Advantages and Disadvantages of Sole Proprietorship Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Easy and inexpensive to form • Profits all go to owner • Direct control of the business • Freedom from government</p><p>• Unlimited personal liability for the</p><p>regulation • No special taxation • Ease of dissolution</p><p>sole proprietor • Difficulty raising capital • Limited managerial expertise • Trouble finding qualified employees • Personal time commitment • Unstable business life • Losses are the owner’s responsibility</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Definition:</b> owned and run by <b>one person</b>; <b>no distinction between business and owner</b>; the owner gets <b>all profits</b> and is responsible for <b>all debts, losses and liabilities</b>; the <b>simplest and most common</b> structure. <b>Advantages:</b> easy and cheap to form; all profits to the owner; direct control; freedom from government regulation; no special taxation; easy to dissolve. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>unlimited personal liability</b>; difficulty raising capital; limited managerial expertise; trouble finding qualified employees; heavy time commitment; unstable business life; losses are the owner's.</p><p class=\"lab lab-E\"><b>Example:</b> A tea stall or a small tailoring shop in Bangladesh is typically a sole proprietorship (trade licence in one person's name).</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>সংজ্ঞা:</b> <b>একজন</b> মালিক ও পরিচালক; <b>ব্যবসা ও মালিকের মধ্যে পার্থক্য নেই</b>; মালিক <b>সব মুনাফা</b> পান এবং <b>সব ঋণ, ক্ষতি ও দায়ের</b> জন্য দায়ী; <b>সবচেয়ে সহজ ও প্রচলিত</b> কাঠামো। <b>সুবিধা:</b> গঠন সহজ ও সস্তা; সব মুনাফা মালিকের; সরাসরি নিয়ন্ত্রণ; সরকারি নিয়ন্ত্রণ থেকে স্বাধীনতা; বিশেষ কর নেই; বন্ধ করা সহজ। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> <b>অসীম ব্যক্তিগত দায়</b>; মূলধন তোলা কঠিন; ব্যবস্থাপনা দক্ষতা সীমিত; যোগ্য কর্মী পাওয়া কঠিন; সময়ের চাপ; অস্থির ব্যবসায়িক জীবন; ক্ষতি মালিকের।</p><p class=\"lab lab-E\"><b>উদাহরণ:</b> বাংলাদেশে চায়ের দোকান বা ছোট দর্জির দোকান সাধারণত একক মালিকানা (একজনের নামে ট্রেড লাইসেন্স)।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s12","k":"slide","t":"Practice question 2","tb":"অনুশীলনী প্রশ্ন ২","sl":[12],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slide 12 of 57 · স্লাইড ১২ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 12) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s12.webp\" alt=\"Slide 12 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Practice Question 2 What would be an advantage of choosing a sole proprietorship over other legal structures of business? A. The sole proprietorship can live long after its founder moves on B. The sole proprietorship is protected from all liability C. The sole proprietorship pays no taxes D. The sole proprietorship would be cheaper to set up</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Answer: D</b> — cheaper to set up. A is wrong (unstable life), B wrong (unlimited liability), C wrong (owner pays personal income tax).</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>উত্তর: D</b> — গঠন সস্তা। A ভুল (জীবন অস্থির), B ভুল (অসীম দায়), C ভুল (মালিক ব্যক্তিগত আয়কর দেন)।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"c7-2","k":"check","t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","sl":[],"h":"","z":{"t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","items":[{"q":"A major disadvantage of a sole proprietorship is…","qbn":"একক মালিকানার প্রধান অসুবিধা…","ans":1,"opts":["complex taxation · জটিল কর","unlimited personal liability · অসীম ব্যক্তিগত দায়","double taxation · দ্বৈত কর","many owners · অনেক মালিক"],"exp":"The owner is personally responsible for all debts and liabilities.","expbn":"মালিক সব ঋণ ও দায়ের জন্য ব্যক্তিগতভাবে দায়ী।"},{"q":"Which is an advantage of a sole proprietorship?","qbn":"একক মালিকানার সুবিধা কোনটি?","ans":1,"opts":["Easy capital raising · সহজে মূলধন তোলা","Direct control and all profits go to the owner · সরাসরি নিয়ন্ত্রণ ও সব মুনাফা মালিকের","Long, stable life · দীর্ঘ স্থিতিশীল জীবন","Shared risk · ভাগ করা ঝুঁকি"],"exp":"Slide 11 advantages.","expbn":"স্লাইড ১১-এর সুবিধা।"}]}},{"id":"q7-3","k":"lesson","t":"Study question 7.3 — Partnerships","tb":"স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৩ — অংশীদারি","sl":[],"h":"<p class=\"lesson-q\"><b>Study question 7.3</b> · স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৩</p><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<p>Slides 13–21.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p>স্লাইড ১৩–২১।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s13","k":"slide","t":"Defining partnerships","tb":"অংশীদারির সংজ্ঞা","sl":[13,14,15],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 13–15 of 57 · স্লাইড ১৩–১৫ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 13) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s13.webp\" alt=\"Slide 13 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s14.webp\" alt=\"Slide 14 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s15.webp\" alt=\"Slide 15 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Partnerships</p><p>Learning Outcomes: Partnerships 7.3: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of partnerships 7.3.1: Define partnerships as a form of business 7.3.2: Describe the difference between general and limited partnerships 7.3.3: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of partnerships</p><p>Defining Partnerships • •</p><p>•</p><p>Partnerships are businesses in which two or more people share ownership and responsibility. Each partner contributes to all aspects of the business, including money, property, labor, or skill. Each partner shares in the profits and losses of the business.</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> A <b>partnership</b> = <b>two or more people share ownership and responsibility</b>. Each partner contributes <b>money, property, labor or skill</b> and shares <b>profits and losses</b>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>অংশীদারি</b> = <b>দুই বা ততোধিক ব্যক্তি মালিকানা ও দায় ভাগ</b> করেন। প্রতিটি অংশীদার <b>টাকা, সম্পত্তি, শ্রম বা দক্ষতা</b> দেন এবং <b>লাভ-ক্ষতি</b> ভাগ করেন।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s16","k":"slide","t":"Types, formation and tax","tb":"ধরন, গঠন ও কর","sl":[16,17],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 16–17 of 57 · স্লাইড ১৬–১৭ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 16) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s16.webp\" alt=\"Slide 16 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s17.webp\" alt=\"Slide 17 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Types of Partnerships General Partnership</p><p>Limited Partnerships (also known as Limited Liability Partnerships)</p><p>•</p><p>•</p><p>•</p><p>Assume that profits, liability, and management duties are divided equally among partners. If you opt for unequal distribution, the percentages assigned to each partner must be documented in the partnership agreement.</p><p>• •</p><p>More complex than general partnerships. Allow partners to have limited liability as well as limited input with management decisions. Limited partnerships are attractive to investors of short-term projects.</p><p>Forming a Partnership and Partnership Taxes Forming a partnership: To form a partnership, you must: • Register your business with the state • Establish your business name • Once your business is registered, you must also obtain licenses and permits Partnership taxes: Most businesses will need to register with the IRS, register with state and local revenue agencies, and obtain a tax ID number. In addition, partnerships must file an annual information return to report income, deductions, gains, and losses from the business’ operations, but the business itself does not pay income tax. Partners include their respective share of the partnership’s income or losses on their personal tax returns.</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b></p><ul><li><b>General partnership:</b> profits, liability and management are <b>divided equally</b> (unequal shares must be written in the <b>partnership agreement</b>); partners have <b>unlimited</b> liability.</li><li><b>Limited partnership (LP/LLP):</b> <b>more complex</b>; partners can have <b>limited liability and limited input in management</b>; attractive to <b>investors in short-term projects</b>.</li><li><b>Forming:</b> register with the state, choose a name, get licences and permits. <b>Tax:</b> the partnership files an <b>information return</b> but <b>does not pay income tax</b>; partners report their share on <b>personal returns</b>.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b></p><ul><li><b>সাধারণ অংশীদারি:</b> লাভ, দায় ও ব্যবস্থাপনা <b>সমানভাবে ভাগ</b> (অসমান ভাগ <b>অংশীদারি চুক্তিতে</b> লিখতে হয়); অংশীদাররা <b>অসীম</b> দায়ী।</li><li><b>সীমিত অংশীদারি (LP/LLP):</b> <b>বেশি জটিল</b>; অংশীদারদের <b>সীমিত দায় ও ব্যবস্থাপনায় সীমিত মতামত</b> থাকতে পারে; <b>স্বল্পমেয়াদি প্রকল্পে বিনিয়োগকারীদের</b> কাছে আকর্ষণীয়।</li><li><b>গঠন:</b> রাজ্যে নিবন্ধন, নাম নির্ধারণ, লাইসেন্স ও অনুমতি। <b>কর:</b> অংশীদারি <b>তথ্য রিটার্ন</b> দেয় কিন্তু <b>আয়কর দেয় না</b>; অংশীদাররা নিজের ভাগ <b>ব্যক্তিগত রিটার্নে</b> দেখান।</li></ul></div></div>"},{"id":"s18","k":"slide","t":"Advantages and disadvantages","tb":"সুবিধা ও অসুবিধা","sl":[18,19],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 18–19 of 57 · স্লাইড ১৮–১৯ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 18) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s18.webp\" alt=\"Slide 18 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s19.webp\" alt=\"Slide 19 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Advantages and Disadvantages of Partnerships Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Easy and inexpensive to form • Shared financial commitment</p><p>• Joint and individual liability • Disagreements among partners • Shared profits</p><p>among partners • Complementary skills / utilize the expertise of each partner • Partnership incentives for employees</p><p>Class Discussion: Going into Business with a Friend • Is it a good idea to form a partnership business with a friend? • What are some of the considerations to think about if you decide to do so?</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Advantages:</b> easy and cheap to form; <b>shared financial commitment</b>; <b>complementary skills</b>; partnership incentives for employees. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>joint and individual liability</b>; <b>disagreements</b> among partners; <b>profits are shared</b>. (Discussion: partnering with a friend works only with a <b>written agreement</b> on roles, money, exit and disputes — friendship does not replace a contract.)</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>সুবিধা:</b> গঠন সহজ ও সস্তা; <b>ভাগ করা আর্থিক দায়িত্ব</b>; <b>পরিপূরক দক্ষতা</b>; কর্মীদের জন্য অংশীদারি প্রণোদনা। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> <b>যৌথ ও ব্যক্তিগত দায়</b>; অংশীদারদের <b>মতভেদ</b>; <b>মুনাফা ভাগ</b>। (আলোচনা: বন্ধুর সাথে অংশীদারি চলে শুধু ভূমিকা, টাকা, বেরোনো ও বিরোধ নিয়ে <b>লিখিত চুক্তি</b> থাকলে — বন্ধুত্ব চুক্তির বিকল্প নয়।)</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s20","k":"slide","t":"Practice questions 3–4","tb":"অনুশীলনী প্রশ্ন ৩–৪","sl":[20,21],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 20–21 of 57 · স্লাইড ২০–২১ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 20) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s20.webp\" alt=\"Slide 20 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s21.webp\" alt=\"Slide 21 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Practice Question 3 Caitlin is invited to join a business as a partner due to her expertise in the field. She is asked to sign a partnership agreement that gives her 40% of the profits, full control of the marketing activities, but final say on all other decisions goes to the original owner. She is joining: A. A limited partnership B. A general partnership C. A dual proprietorship D. An S corporation</p><p>Practice Question 4 The following are all advantages of business partnerships EXCEPT: A. Partnerships shield the individual partners from debt and liability B. Partnerships are relatively easy and inexpensive to set up C. Partnerships pool the resources of the partners to obtain capital D. Partnerships can take advantage of the various skills, strengths, and experiences of each of the partners</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Q3: B — a general partnership</b> (Caitlin has a share of profits and some control, no limited-liability or investor-only role mentioned; she signs a partnership agreement). <b>Q4: A</b> — partnerships do <b>not</b> shield partners from debt and liability (that is the exception).</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>প্রশ্ন ৩: B — সাধারণ অংশীদারি</b> (লাভের অংশ ও কিছু নিয়ন্ত্রণ আছে; সীমিত দায়ের উল্লেখ নেই; অংশীদারি চুক্তি করছে)। <b>প্রশ্ন ৪: A</b> — অংশীদারি অংশীদারদের ঋণ ও দায় থেকে রক্ষা <b>করে না</b> (এটিই ব্যতিক্রম)।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"c7-3","k":"check","t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","sl":[],"h":"","z":{"t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","items":[{"q":"Partners in a general partnership have…","qbn":"সাধারণ অংশীদারিতে অংশীদারদের আছে…","ans":1,"opts":["no liability · কোনো দায় নেই","unlimited, joint liability · অসীম, যৌথ দায়","tax paid by the partnership · অংশীদারির দেওয়া কর","no management role · ব্যবস্থাপনার ভূমিকা নেই"],"exp":"Partners share profits, losses and liability.","expbn":"অংশীদাররা লাভ, ক্ষতি ও দায় ভাগ করেন।"},{"q":"How are partnership profits taxed?","qbn":"অংশীদারির মুনাফার কর কীভাবে হয়?","ans":0,"opts":["Partners report their share on personal returns; the partnership itself pays no income tax · অংশীদাররা ব্যক্তিগত রিটার্নে নিজের ভাগ দেখান; অংশীদারি নিজে আয়কর দেয় না","Taxed twice · দুইবার কর","Not taxed at all · মোটেই কর নেই","Only the largest partner pays · শুধু বড় অংশীদার দেয়"],"exp":"Pass-through: the partnership files an information return.","expbn":"পাস-থ্রু: অংশীদারি তথ্য রিটার্ন দেয়।"}]}},{"id":"q7-4","k":"lesson","t":"Study question 7.4 — Corporations","tb":"স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৪ — কর্পোরেশন","sl":[],"h":"<p class=\"lesson-q\"><b>Study question 7.4</b> · স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৪</p><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<p>Slides 22–32.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p>স্লাইড ২২–৩২।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s22","k":"slide","t":"Corporate personhood and types","tb":"কর্পোরেট ব্যক্তিত্ব ও ধরন","sl":[22,23,24,25],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 22–25 of 57 · স্লাইড ২২–২৫ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 22) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s22.webp\" alt=\"Slide 22 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s23.webp\" alt=\"Slide 23 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s24.webp\" alt=\"Slide 24 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s25.webp\" alt=\"Slide 25 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Corporations</p><p>Learning Outcomes: Corporations 7.4: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of corporations 7.4.1: Summarize the difference between C and S corporations 7.4.2: Explain the purpose and requirements of a benefit corporations (B corp) 7.4.3: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of corporations</p><p>Background on Corporate Rights Corporate personhood: the legal notion that corporations, apart from their associated human beings (like owners, managers, or employees), have some, but not all, of the legal rights and responsibilities enjoyed by natural persons (physical humans). Corporations have the right to enter into contracts with other parties and to sue or be sued in court in the same way as natural persons or unincorporated associations of persons. Since the Supreme Court’s ruling in Citizens United v. Federal Election Commission in 2010, upholding the rights of corporations to make political expenditures under the First Amendment, there have been several calls for a U.S. Constitutional amendment to abolish corporate personhood. While the Citizens United majority opinion makes no reference to corporate personhood or the Fourteenth Amendment, Justice Stevens’ dissent claims that the majority opinion relies on an incorrect treatment of corporations’ First Amendment rights as identical to those of individuals.</p><p>Types of Corporations Three types of corporations: 1. C corporations 2. S corporations 3. B corporations</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Corporate personhood</b> = a corporation, apart from its owners, has <b>some but not all</b> legal rights of a person: it can <b>make contracts and sue or be sued</b>. (After <b>Citizens United v. FEC, 2010</b>, corporations can make political expenditures under the First Amendment; some want to abolish corporate personhood.) Three types: <b>C, S and B corporations</b>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>কর্পোরেট ব্যক্তিত্ব</b> = কর্পোরেশন, মালিকদের থেকে আলাদা, একজন মানুষের <b>কিছু কিন্তু সব নয়</b> আইনি অধিকার রাখে: <b>চুক্তি করতে এবং মামলা করতে বা মামলার বিবাদী হতে</b> পারে। (<b>সিটিজেনস ইউনাইটেড বনাম FEC, ২০১০</b>-এর পর কর্পোরেশন প্রথম সংশোধনীর অধীনে রাজনৈতিক ব্যয় করতে পারে; কেউ কেউ কর্পোরেট ব্যক্তিত্ব বিলোপ চায়।) তিন ধরন: <b>C, S ও B কর্পোরেশন</b>।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s26","k":"slide","t":"C corporations","tb":"C কর্পোরেশন","sl":[26,27],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 26–27 of 57 · স্লাইড ২৬–২৭ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=26\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 26) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s26.webp\" alt=\"Slide 26 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s27.webp\" alt=\"Slide 27 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>C Corporations • Independent legal entities owned by shareholders • More complex than other business structures because of • •</p><p>•</p><p>Costly administrative fees</p><p>•</p><p>Complex tax and legal requirements</p><p>When you form a corporation, you form a separate tax paying entity, unlike sole proprietorships or partnerships Income paid as dividends is taxed twice</p><p>Advantages and Disadvantages of C Corps Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Limited liability: shareholder’s personal assets are protected. Shareholders can generally only be held responsible for their investment in stock in the company</p><p>• Time and money: costly and time consuming to start and operate</p><p>• Ability to generate capital through sale of stock</p><p>• Corporate tax treatment: Corporations file taxes separately from their owners. • Attractive to potential employees</p><p>• Double taxing: In some cases, corporations are taxed twice—first, when the company makes a profit, and again when dividends are paid to shareholders.</p><p>• Additional paperwork: There are increased paperwork and recordkeeping burdens associated with this entity.</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>C corporation</b> = an <b>independent legal entity owned by shareholders</b>; <b>more complex</b> (costly fees, complex tax and legal rules); a <b>separate tax-paying entity</b>; dividends are <b>taxed twice</b>. <b>Advantages:</b> <b>limited liability</b> (shareholders lose only their investment); <b>can raise capital by selling stock</b>; corporate tax treatment; attractive to employees. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>costly and time-consuming</b> to start and run; <b>double taxation</b> (company profit, then shareholder dividends); <b>more paperwork</b>.</p><p class=\"lab lab-E\"><b>Example:</b> Grameenphone, Square Pharma and BRAC Bank are corporations owned by many shareholders.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>C কর্পোরেশন</b> = <b>শেয়ারহোল্ডারদের মালিকানাধীন স্বাধীন আইনি সত্তা</b>; <b>বেশি জটিল</b> (ব্যয়বহুল ফি, জটিল কর ও আইনি নিয়ম); <b>আলাদা করদাতা সত্তা</b>; লভ্যাংশে <b>দুইবার কর</b>। <b>সুবিধা:</b> <b>সীমিত দায়</b> (শেয়ারহোল্ডার শুধু বিনিয়োগ হারান); <b>শেয়ার বেচে মূলধন তোলা যায়</b>; কর্পোরেট কর ব্যবস্থা; কর্মীদের কাছে আকর্ষণীয়। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> শুরু ও চালানো <b>ব্যয়বহুল ও সময়সাপেক্ষ</b>; <b>দ্বৈত কর</b> (কোম্পানির মুনাফা, তারপর শেয়ারহোল্ডারের লভ্যাংশ); <b>বেশি কাগজপত্র</b>।</p><p class=\"lab lab-E\"><b>উদাহরণ:</b> গ্রামীণফোন, স্কয়ার ফার্মা ও ব্র্যাক ব্যাংক অনেক শেয়ারহোল্ডারের মালিকানাধীন কর্পোরেশন।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s28","k":"slide","t":"S corporations","tb":"S কর্পোরেশন","sl":[28,29],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 28–29 of 57 · স্লাইড ২৮–২৯ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=28\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 28) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s28.webp\" alt=\"Slide 28 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s29.webp\" alt=\"Slide 29 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>S Corporations • Special type of corporation created through an IRS tax election • An eligible domestic corporation can avoid double taxation by electing to</p><p>be treated as an S corporation • Profits and losses can pass through to your personal tax return • The business is not taxed; instead, only the shareholders are taxed • Any shareholder who works for the company must pay herself a “reasonable compensation”</p><p>Advantages and Disadvantages of S Corps Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Tax savings: Only the wages of the S corp shareholder who is an employee are subject to employment tax.</p><p>• Stricter operational processes: As a separate structure, S corps require scheduled director and shareholder meetings, minutes from those meetings, adoption and updates to by-laws, stock transfers, and records maintenance.</p><p>• Business expense tax credits: Some expenses that shareholder/employees incur can be written off as business expenses. • Independent life: An S corp designation also allows a business to have an independent life, separate from its shareholders.</p><p>• Shareholder compensation requirements: A shareholder must receive reasonable compensation.</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>S corporation</b> = a special type created by an <b>IRS tax election</b> so an eligible domestic corporation can <b>avoid double taxation</b>: profits and losses <b>pass through to personal returns</b>; <b>only shareholders are taxed</b>; a shareholder-employee must be paid a <b>\"reasonable compensation\"</b>. <b>Advantages:</b> <b>tax savings</b> (only wages are subject to employment tax); expense write-offs; <b>independent life</b> separate from shareholders. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>stricter processes</b> (meetings, minutes, by-laws, stock transfers, records); <b>reasonable compensation</b> requirement.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>S কর্পোরেশন</b> = <b>IRS কর নির্বাচনে</b> তৈরি বিশেষ ধরন, যাতে যোগ্য দেশীয় কর্পোরেশন <b>দ্বৈত কর এড়াতে</b> পারে: মুনাফা-ক্ষতি <b>ব্যক্তিগত রিটার্নে চলে যায়</b>; <b>শুধু শেয়ারহোল্ডার করদাতা</b>; শেয়ারহোল্ডার-কর্মীকে <b>\"যুক্তিসঙ্গত পারিশ্রমিক\"</b> দিতে হয়। <b>সুবিধা:</b> <b>কর সাশ্রয়</b> (শুধু বেতনে কর্মসংস্থান কর); ব্যয় বাদ; শেয়ারহোল্ডারদের থেকে <b>আলাদা জীবন</b>। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> <b>কড়া প্রক্রিয়া</b> (সভা, কার্যবিবরণী, বিধি, শেয়ার হস্তান্তর, নথি); <b>যুক্তিসঙ্গত পারিশ্রমিক</b> বাধ্যবাধকতা।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s30","k":"slide","t":"Benefit (B) corporations","tb":"বেনিফিট (B) কর্পোরেশন","sl":[30,31],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 30–31 of 57 · স্লাইড ৩০–৩১ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=30\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 30) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s30.webp\" alt=\"Slide 30 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s31.webp\" alt=\"Slide 31 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Benefit (B) Corporations •</p><p>Type of for-profit corporate entity, authorized by thirty U.S. states and the District of Columbia, that creates a general public benefit, which is defined as a material positive impact on society and the environment. This can include positive impact on society, workers, the community, and the environment.</p><p>•</p><p>Transparency provisions require benefit corporations to publish annual benefit reports on their social and environmental performance using a comprehensive, credible, independent, and transparent third-party-standard.</p><p>•</p><p>Differ from traditional C corporations in purpose, accountability, and transparency, but not in taxation. B Corps elect to be taxed as a C or an S corp.</p><p>Advantages and Disadvantages of B Corps Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Protection of mission: Becoming a B Corp gives companies more options and protections if they decide to sell the business to someone else or take it public</p><p>• Transparency and reporting requirements: B Corps must provide an annual benefit report according to a third-party standard and make the report available on their company Websites.</p><p>• Reputation: B Corps stand out as businesses that have a social conscience and aspire to a standard they consider higher than maximizing profit</p><p>• Creation of value: B Corps may create value via employee engagement and customer loyalty, thereby improving results for all stakeholders</p><p>• Annual fees to retain certified B Corp status • Compliance and governance obligations: Most states require publicly traded companies with a B corp designation to have a “benefit director” who is responsible for ensuring that the corporation meets its stated public purpose.</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>B corporation</b> = a <b>for-profit</b> entity (authorized in <b>30 US states + DC</b>) that creates a <b>general public benefit</b> — a <b>material positive impact on society and the environment</b>. It must publish an <b>annual benefit report</b> using an independent third-party standard. It differs from a C corp in <b>purpose, accountability and transparency, not taxation</b> (it is taxed as a C or S corp). <b>Advantages:</b> <b>mission protection</b> when selling or going public; <b>reputation</b>; <b>value creation</b> via employee engagement and loyalty. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>reporting requirements</b>; <b>annual fees</b>; <b>governance obligations</b> (a \"benefit director\").</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>B কর্পোরেশন</b> = <b>মুনাফাভিত্তিক</b> সত্তা (<b>৩০টি মার্কিন রাজ্য + DC</b>-এ অনুমোদিত) যা <b>সাধারণ জনকল্যাণ</b> তৈরি করে — <b>সমাজ ও পরিবেশে বস্তুগত ইতিবাচক প্রভাব</b>। স্বাধীন তৃতীয় পক্ষের মান অনুযায়ী <b>বার্ষিক সুবিধা প্রতিবেদন</b> প্রকাশ করতে হয়। C কর্পোরেশন থেকে পার্থক্য <b>উদ্দেশ্য, জবাবদিহি ও স্বচ্ছতায়, করে নয়</b> (C বা S হিসেবেই কর)। <b>সুবিধা:</b> বিক্রি বা পাবলিক হওয়ার সময় <b>লক্ষ্যের সুরক্ষা</b>; <b>সুনাম</b>; কর্মী সম্পৃক্ততা ও আনুগত্যে <b>মূল্য সৃষ্টি</b>। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> <b>প্রতিবেদনের শর্ত</b>; <b>বার্ষিক ফি</b>; <b>পরিচালনার দায়</b> (\"বেনিফিট ডিরেক্টর\")।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s32","k":"slide","t":"Practice question 5","tb":"অনুশীলনী প্রশ্ন ৫","sl":[32],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slide 32 of 57 · স্লাইড ৩২ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 32) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s32.webp\" alt=\"Slide 32 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Practice Question 5 The most significant differences between C and S corporations have to do with: A. Supply chain structure, compliance standards, and taxation B. Taxation, operation, and incorporations C. Administration, employee benefits, and taxation D. Taxation, administration, and shareholder compensation</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Answer: D — taxation, administration and shareholder compensation.</b> S corp: no double tax, stricter administration, reasonable-compensation rule.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>উত্তর: D — কর, প্রশাসন ও শেয়ারহোল্ডারের পারিশ্রমিক।</b> S কর্পোরেশন: দ্বৈত কর নেই, কড়া প্রশাসন, যুক্তিসঙ্গত পারিশ্রমিকের নিয়ম।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"c7-4","k":"check","t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","sl":[],"h":"","z":{"t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","items":[{"q":"\"Double taxation\" is mainly a problem of…","qbn":"\"দ্বৈত কর\" মূলত সমস্যা…","ans":1,"opts":["sole proprietorships · একক মালিকানার","C corporations · C কর্পোরেশনের","S corporations · S কর্পোরেশনের","LLPs · LLP-র"],"exp":"C-corp profit is taxed, then dividends are taxed again.","expbn":"C কর্পোরেশনের মুনাফায় কর, তারপর লভ্যাংশে আবার কর।"},{"q":"A key advantage of the corporate form is…","qbn":"কর্পোরেট রূপের মূল সুবিধা…","ans":1,"opts":["no paperwork · কোনো কাগজপত্র নেই","limited liability and ability to raise capital by selling stock · সীমিত দায় ও শেয়ার বেচে মূলধন তোলার সক্ষমতা","no taxes · কোনো কর নেই","owner keeps all control · মালিকের পূর্ণ নিয়ন্ত্রণ"],"exp":"Shareholders risk only their investment; stock sales raise capital.","expbn":"শেয়ারহোল্ডাররা শুধু বিনিয়োগ ঝুঁকিতে রাখেন; শেয়ার বেচে মূলধন ওঠে।"},{"q":"A benefit (B) corporation must…","qbn":"বেনিফিট (B) কর্পোরেশনকে অবশ্যই…","ans":1,"opts":["be a nonprofit · অলাভজনক হতে হবে","create a general public benefit and publish an annual benefit report · সাধারণ জনকল্যাণ সৃষ্টি ও বার্ষিক সুবিধা প্রতিবেদন প্রকাশ করতে হবে","pay no tax · কর দেবে না","avoid shareholders · শেয়ারহোল্ডার এড়াবে"],"exp":"B corps are for-profit and must report on their social and environmental performance.","expbn":"B কর্পোরেশন মুনাফাভিত্তিক এবং সামাজিক-পরিবেশগত কর্মক্ষমতা প্রতিবেদন করতে হয়।"}]}},{"id":"q7-5","k":"lesson","t":"Study question 7.5 — Hybrid forms: LLC and LLP","tb":"স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৫ — হাইব্রিড রূপ: LLC ও LLP","sl":[],"h":"<p class=\"lesson-q\"><b>Study question 7.5</b> · স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৫</p><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<p>Slides 33–40.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p>স্লাইড ৩৩–৪০।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s33","k":"slide","t":"Limited liability company (LLC)","tb":"সীমিত দায় কোম্পানি (LLC)","sl":[33,34,35,36],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 33–36 of 57 · স্লাইড ৩৩–৩৬ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=33\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 33) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s33.webp\" alt=\"Slide 33 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s34.webp\" alt=\"Slide 34 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s35.webp\" alt=\"Slide 35 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s36.webp\" alt=\"Slide 36 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Hybrid Forms of Ownership</p><p>Learning Outcomes: Hybrid Forms of Ownership 7.5: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of hybrid forms of business ownership 7.5.1: Define limited liability company (LLC) as a form of business 7.5.2: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of LLCs 7.5.3: Define limited liability partnerships (LLP) as a form of business 7.5.4: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of LLPs</p><p>LLC (Limited Liability Company) • Hybrid business structure allowed by state statute • Provides the limited liability features of a corporation • Provides tax efficiencies and operational flexibility of partnerships • Owners of an LLC are called members. • Unlike shareholders in a corporation, LLCs are not taxed as a separate</p><p>business entity: instead profits and losses are “passed through” the business to each member of the LLC</p><p>Advantages and Disadvantages of an LLC Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Limited Liability: Members are</p><p>• Possible Limited Life: When an LLC is formed, the members must decide on the duration of the LLC. • Self Employment Taxes: Members of an LLC are considered self-employed and must pay the self-employment tax contributions towards Medicare and Social Security.</p><p>•</p><p>protected from personal liability for business decisions Less Record Keeping compared to an S Corporation</p><p>• Sharing of Profits: Members distribute profits as they see fit. It’s up to the members to decide who has earned what percentage of the profits or losses</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>LLC</b> = a <b>hybrid structure</b> allowed by <b>state statute</b>: the <b>limited liability of a corporation</b> + the <b>tax efficiency and flexibility of a partnership</b>. Owners are <b>members</b>. The LLC is <b>not taxed as a separate entity</b> — profits and losses <b>pass through</b> to members. <b>Advantages:</b> <b>limited liability</b>; <b>less record-keeping</b> than an S corp; members <b>share profits as they decide</b>. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>possibly limited life</b> (members decide duration); <b>self-employment taxes</b> (Medicare and Social Security).</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>LLC</b> = <b>রাজ্যের আইনে অনুমোদিত হাইব্রিড কাঠামো</b>: <b>কর্পোরেশনের সীমিত দায়</b> + <b>অংশীদারির কর সুবিধা ও নমনীয়তা</b>। মালিকরা <b>সদস্য</b>। LLC <b>আলাদা সত্তা হিসেবে করযোগ্য নয়</b> — লাভ-ক্ষতি সদস্যদের কাছে <b>চলে যায়</b>। <b>সুবিধা:</b> <b>সীমিত দায়</b>; S কর্পোরেশনের চেয়ে <b>কম নথি রাখা</b>; সদস্যরা <b>নিজেদের সিদ্ধান্তে মুনাফা ভাগ</b> করেন। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> <b>সম্ভাব্য সীমিত জীবন</b> (সদস্যরা মেয়াদ ঠিক করেন); <b>স্ব-কর্মসংস্থান কর</b> (মেডিকেয়ার ও সোশ্যাল সিকিউরিটি)।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s37","k":"slide","t":"Limited liability partnership (LLP)","tb":"সীমিত দায় অংশীদারি (LLP)","sl":[37,38],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 37–38 of 57 · স্লাইড ৩৭–৩৮ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=37\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 37) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s37.webp\" alt=\"Slide 37 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s38.webp\" alt=\"Slide 38 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>LLP (Limited Liability Partnership) • A partnership in which some or all partners have limited liabilities • One partner is not responsible or liable for another partner’s misconduct or negligence • Some states require one partner to be a “general partner” with unlimited liability • Partners may manage the company directly without electing a board of directors • Profits are allocated among the partners for tax purposes, avoiding the problem of “double taxation” often found in corporations</p><p>Advantages and Disadvantages of an LLP Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Single taxation: The credits and deductions of the company are passed through to partners to file on their individual tax returns. • Limited liability: The LLP structure protects individual limited partners from personal liability for negligent acts of other partners or employees not under their direct control. • Flexibility: LLPs provide the partners flexibility in business ownership.</p><p>• Duration: The business life of an LLP is</p><p>unstable. • Limitations of formation: Limited liability partnerships are not recognized as legal business structures in every state. • Partner control: If an LLP is formed without a limited liability partnership agreement, individual partners are not obligated to consult with other participants in certain business agreements.</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>LLP</b> = a partnership in which <b>some or all partners have limited liability</b>: <b>one partner is not liable for another's misconduct or negligence</b>; some states require one <b>general partner</b> with unlimited liability; partners can <b>manage directly</b>; profits are allocated for tax, <b>avoiding double taxation</b>. <b>Advantages:</b> <b>single taxation</b>; <b>limited liability</b> from others' negligence; <b>flexibility</b>. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>unstable business life</b>; <b>not recognized in every state</b>; without an agreement a partner <b>need not consult others</b> on certain deals.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>LLP</b> = এমন অংশীদারি যেখানে <b>কিছু বা সব অংশীদারের সীমিত দায়</b>: <b>একজন অন্যের অন্যায় বা অবহেলার জন্য দায়ী নন</b>; কিছু রাজ্যে অসীম দায়ের একজন <b>সাধারণ অংশীদার</b> লাগে; অংশীদাররা <b>সরাসরি পরিচালনা</b> করতে পারেন; কর ঠিক করতে মুনাফা বণ্টিত হয়, <b>দ্বৈত কর এড়ানো যায়</b>। <b>সুবিধা:</b> <b>একক কর</b>; অন্যের অবহেলা থেকে <b>সীমিত দায়</b>; <b>নমনীয়তা</b>। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> <b>অস্থির ব্যবসায়িক জীবন</b>; <b>সব রাজ্যে স্বীকৃত নয়</b>; চুক্তি না থাকলে কিছু বিষয়ে অংশীদার <b>অন্যদের সাথে পরামর্শ করতে বাধ্য নয়</b>।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s39","k":"slide","t":"Practice questions 6–7","tb":"অনুশীলনী প্রশ্ন ৬–৭","sl":[39,40],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 39–40 of 57 · স্লাইড ৩৯–৪০ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=39\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 39) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s39.webp\" alt=\"Slide 39 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s40.webp\" alt=\"Slide 40 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Practice Question 6 Warren is starting a business. His biggest concerns are losing everything he owns if something goes wrong and being mired in strict taxation and administrative regulations. For those reasons, he decides to start a(n): A. C Corporation B. S Corporation C. Sole Proprietorship D. LLC</p><p>Practice Question 7 This business legal structure can be defined as having single taxation, limited liability, and the flexibility to let each individual in the business decide how much responsibility and participation they want. This is a(n): A. LLP B. LLC C. B Corp D. C Corp</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Q6: D — LLC</b> (limited liability, without strict corporate taxation and administration). <b>Q7: A — LLP</b>, per the slide: single taxation, limited liability and flexibility on each person's responsibility and participation.</p><p class=\"lab lab-K\"><b>Exam tip:</b> Trap: LLC (owners = members, corporate-style liability) vs LLP (partners). The slide's practice answer for Q7 is <b>LLP</b> because of \"partners decide how much responsibility they want\".</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>প্রশ্ন ৬: D — LLC</b> (সীমিত দায়, কড়া কর্পোরেট কর ও প্রশাসন ছাড়া)। <b>প্রশ্ন ৭: A — LLP</b>, স্লাইড অনুযায়ী: একক কর, সীমিত দায় ও প্রতিজনের দায় ও অংশগ্রহণে নমনীয়তা।</p><p class=\"lab lab-K\"><b>পরীক্ষার টিপস:</b> ফাঁদ: LLC (মালিক = সদস্য) বনাম LLP (অংশীদার)। Q7-এ স্লাইডের উত্তর <b>LLP</b> কারণ \"অংশীদাররা কতটা দায় চান তা ঠিক করেন\"।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"c7-5","k":"check","t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","sl":[],"h":"","z":{"t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","items":[{"q":"The owners of an LLC are called…","qbn":"LLC-র মালিকদের বলা হয়…","ans":2,"opts":["shareholders · শেয়ারহোল্ডার","partners · অংশীদার","members · সদস্য","franchisees · ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজি"],"exp":"LLC owners are called members.","expbn":"LLC-র মালিকরা সদস্য।"},{"q":"An LLC combines…","qbn":"LLC একত্র করে…","ans":0,"opts":["limited liability of a corporation with the tax flexibility of a partnership · কর্পোরেশনের সীমিত দায় ও অংশীদারির কর নমনীয়তা","unlimited liability with double tax · অসীম দায় ও দ্বৈত কর","sole control with no tax · পূর্ণ নিয়ন্ত্রণ ও করমুক্তি","franchise rights with a patent · ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ অধিকার ও পেটেন্ট"],"exp":"It is a hybrid: corporate liability protection plus partnership-style pass-through taxation.","expbn":"এটি হাইব্রিড: কর্পোরেট দায়-সুরক্ষা ও অংশীদারির মতো পাস-থ্রু কর।"},{"q":"In an LLP, one partner is…","qbn":"LLP-তে একজন অংশীদার…","ans":1,"opts":["liable for all partners · সব অংশীদারের জন্য দায়ী","not responsible for another partner's misconduct or negligence · অন্য অংশীদারের অন্যায় বা অবহেলার জন্য দায়ী নন","always unlimited · সবসময় অসীম দায়ী","never taxed · কখনো করযোগ্য নন"],"exp":"That is the key protection of an LLP.","expbn":"এটিই LLP-র মূল সুরক্ষা।"}]}},{"id":"q7-6","k":"lesson","t":"Study question 7.6 — Franchises","tb":"স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৬ — ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ","sl":[],"h":"<p class=\"lesson-q\"><b>Study question 7.6</b> · স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৬</p><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<p>Slides 41–47.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p>স্লাইড ৪১–৪৭।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s41","k":"slide","t":"Defining franchises","tb":"ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজের সংজ্ঞা","sl":[41,42,43],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 41–43 of 57 · স্লাইড ৪১–৪৩ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=41\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 41) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s41.webp\" alt=\"Slide 41 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s42.webp\" alt=\"Slide 42 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s43.webp\" alt=\"Slide 43 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Franchises</p><p>Learning Outcomes: Franchises 7.6: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of franchises 7.6.1: Discuss franchises as a form of business 7.6.2: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of franchising for the franchisee 7.6.3: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of franchising for the franchisor</p><p>Defining Franchises A franchise is a business model that involves one business owner (the franchisor) licensing trademarks and methods to an independent entrepreneur (the franchisee) for a prescribed period of time.</p><p>For the franchisor, the franchise is an alternative to expanding through the establishment of a new location, which avoids the financial investment and liability of a chain of stores.</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> A <b>franchise</b> = a business model where the <b>franchisor</b> licenses <b>trademarks and methods</b> to an independent entrepreneur, the <b>franchisee</b>, for a <b>set period</b>. For the franchisor it is an <b>alternative to opening new locations</b>, avoiding the <b>investment and liability</b> of a chain.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ</b> = এমন ব্যবসা মডেল যেখানে <b>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজর</b> একজন স্বাধীন উদ্যোক্তা, <b>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজিকে</b>, <b>নির্দিষ্ট সময়ের</b> জন্য <b>ট্রেডমার্ক ও পদ্ধতি</b> লাইসেন্স দেয়। ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজরের জন্য এটি <b>নতুন শাখা খোলার বিকল্প</b>, চেইনের <b>বিনিয়োগ ও দায় এড়ানো</b> যায়।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s44","k":"slide","t":"Advantages and disadvantages","tb":"সুবিধা ও অসুবিধা","sl":[44,45],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 44–45 of 57 · স্লাইড ৪৪–৪৫ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=44\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 44) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s44.webp\" alt=\"Slide 44 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s45.webp\" alt=\"Slide 45 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Advantages and Disadvantages for the Franchisee Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Less risk • Name/brand recognition: The franchise has an established image and identity already, which can reduce or simplify marketing efforts. • Access to expertise, ongoing support: Franchisee often receives help with site selection, training materials, product supply, and marketing plans. • Relative autonomy</p><p>• Cost: Buying and running a franchise can be very expensive. • Unequal partnership: The franchisor sets the rules, and the franchisee must follow them. • Rules and enforcement: Franchisor rules imposed by the franchising authority are becoming increasingly strict. Some franchisors are using minor rule violations to terminate contracts and seize the franchise without any reimbursement.</p><p>Advantages and Disadvantages for the Franchisor Advantages</p><p>Disadvantages</p><p>• Access to capital for growth and expansion • Cash flow for operations: In addition to initial franchise fees that can range from $50,000 to $5 million, franchisors receive payments in the form of royalties from each franchisee.</p><p>• Lack of control: Despite the language of the franchise agreement, once the franchisee has established their location, the franchisor may have difficulty ensuring that quality standards are met and the franchise is operating in a manner that benefits the brand.</p><p>• Economies of scale: Once a franchise is established with multiple locations, the company may be able to leverage its buying power to realize economies of scale with suppliers, advertisers, and vendors.</p><p>• Trade secrets: If the success of a business is based on a trade secret, special process, or innovative technology, establishing a franchise may make the business vulnerable to knock-offs or imitation. • Overexposure / Brand Dilution</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Franchisee — advantages:</b> <b>less risk</b>; <b>brand recognition</b>; <b>expertise and ongoing support</b> (site, training, supply, marketing); <b>relative autonomy</b>. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>cost</b>; <b>unequal partnership</b> (franchisor sets rules); <b>strict rules and enforcement</b> (contracts may be terminated for minor violations). <b>Franchisor — advantages:</b> <b>capital for growth</b>; <b>cash flow</b> (initial fees $50,000–$5 million plus <b>royalties</b>); <b>economies of scale</b>. <b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>lack of control</b> over quality; <b>trade secrets</b> exposed; <b>overexposure / brand dilution</b>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজি — সুবিধা:</b> <b>কম ঝুঁকি</b>; <b>ব্র্যান্ড পরিচিতি</b>; <b>দক্ষতা ও ধারাবাহিক সহায়তা</b> (স্থান, প্রশিক্ষণ, সরবরাহ, মার্কেটিং); <b>আপেক্ষিক স্বায়ত্তশাসন</b>। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> <b>খরচ</b>; <b>অসম অংশীদারি</b> (নিয়ম ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজর ঠিক করেন); <b>কড়া নিয়ম ও প্রয়োগ</b> (ছোট লঙ্ঘনেও চুক্তি বাতিল হতে পারে)। <b>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজর — সুবিধা:</b> <b>বৃদ্ধির মূলধন</b>; <b>নগদ প্রবাহ</b> (প্রাথমিক ফি $৫০,০০০–$৫ মিলিয়ন ও <b>রয়্যালটি</b>); <b>বৃহদায়তনের সুবিধা</b>। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> মানের উপর <b>নিয়ন্ত্রণের অভাব</b>; <b>ব্যবসায়িক গোপনীয়তা</b> ঝুঁকিতে; <b>অতিরিক্ত প্রসার / ব্র্যান্ড ক্ষয়</b>।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s46","k":"slide","t":"Practice questions 8–9","tb":"অনুশীলনী প্রশ্ন ৮–৯","sl":[46,47],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 46–47 of 57 · স্লাইড ৪৬–৪৭ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=46\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 46) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s46.webp\" alt=\"Slide 46 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s47.webp\" alt=\"Slide 47 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Practice Question 8 The advantages of being a franchise are: A. Risk reduction, brand recognition, and no royalty payments B. Risk reduction, brand recognition, and relative autonomy C. Brand recognition, no initial investment, and access to expertise D. Access to expertise, relative autonomy, and startup funds</p><p>Practice Question 9 These are the primary disadvantages for the Franchisor in a franchise business model. A. Vulnerability of trade secrets, high cost of entry, and lack of control B. Increased investment risk, lack of control, and overexposure of the brand C. Lack of control, vulnerability of trade secrets, and overexposure of the brand D. Increased tax rate, lack of control, and overexposure of the brand</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Q8: B</b> — risk reduction, brand recognition, relative autonomy. <b>Q9: C</b> — lack of control, vulnerability of trade secrets, overexposure of the brand.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>প্রশ্ন ৮: B</b> — ঝুঁকি হ্রাস, ব্র্যান্ড পরিচিতি, আপেক্ষিক স্বায়ত্তশাসন। <b>প্রশ্ন ৯: C</b> — নিয়ন্ত্রণের অভাব, গোপনীয়তা ঝুঁকি, ব্র্যান্ডের অতিরিক্ত প্রসার।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"c7-6","k":"check","t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","sl":[],"h":"","z":{"t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","items":[{"q":"A franchisor's disadvantage is…","qbn":"ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজরের অসুবিধা…","ans":1,"opts":["no cash flow · নগদ প্রবাহ নেই","lack of control over quality and risk of brand dilution · মানের উপর নিয়ন্ত্রণের অভাব ও ব্র্যান্ড ক্ষয়ের ঝুঁকি","no royalties · রয়্যালটি নেই","no growth · বৃদ্ধি নেই"],"exp":"Slide 45 disadvantages.","expbn":"স্লাইড ৪৫-এর অসুবিধা।"},{"q":"A franchisee gets…","qbn":"ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজি পায়…","ans":0,"opts":["brand recognition and ongoing support · ব্র্যান্ড পরিচিতি ও ধারাবাহিক সহায়তা","all rules waived · সব নিয়ম মওকুফ","no fees · কোনো ফি নেই","the franchisor's profit · ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজরের মুনাফা"],"exp":"Established brand plus training and support reduce risk.","expbn":"প্রতিষ্ঠিত ব্র্যান্ড, প্রশিক্ষণ ও সহায়তা ঝুঁকি কমায়।"}]}},{"id":"q7-7","k":"lesson","t":"Study question 7.7 — Mergers and acquisitions","tb":"স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৭ — একীভূতকরণ ও অধিগ্রহণ","sl":[],"h":"<p class=\"lesson-q\"><b>Study question 7.7</b> · স্টাডি প্রশ্ন ৭.৭</p><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<p>Slides 48–57.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p>স্লাইড ৪৮–৫৭।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s48","k":"slide","t":"Mergers","tb":"একীভূতকরণ","sl":[48,49,50,51],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 48–51 of 57 · স্লাইড ৪৮–৫১ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=48\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 48) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s48.webp\" alt=\"Slide 48 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s49.webp\" alt=\"Slide 49 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s50.webp\" alt=\"Slide 50 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s51.webp\" alt=\"Slide 51 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Mergers and Acquisitions</p><p>Learning Outcomes: Mergers and Acquisitions 7.7: Describe the two types of mergers and acquisitions 7.7.1: Define merger as a business strategy 7.7.2: Define acquisition as a business strategy 7.7.3: Explain why companies undertake horizontal mergers and acquisitions 7.7.4: Explain why companies undertake vertical mergers and acquisitions</p><p>Defining Mergers • A merger is the consolidation of two</p><p>companies that, prior to the merger, were operating as independent entities. • A merger usually creates one larger company, and one of the original companies ceases to exist. • Mergers can be either horizontal or vertical.</p><p>Two Types of Mergers Horizontal</p><p>Vertical</p><p>•</p><p>•</p><p>• •</p><p>Occurs between companies in the same industry A consolidation of two or more businesses that operated in the same market space, often as competitors Common in industries with fewer firms where competition tends to be higher</p><p>• •</p><p>A merger of two organizations that have a buyer-seller relationship or Two or more firms that are operating at different levels within an industry’s supply chain Logic behind the merger is often that the two firms would operate more efficiently together rather than separately</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> A <b>merger</b> = <b>consolidation of two independent companies</b>; usually <b>one larger company</b> results and <b>one original ceases to exist</b>. Two types:</p>\n<ul><li><b>Horizontal</b> — between companies in the <b>same industry</b>, often <b>competitors</b>; common where there are <b>few firms</b>.</li><li><b>Vertical</b> — between firms with a <b>buyer–seller relationship</b>, at <b>different levels of the supply chain</b>; logic: they <b>operate more efficiently together</b>.</li></ul><p class=\"lab lab-E\"><b>Example:</b> Horizontal: two mobile operators merge (Robi + Airtel Bangladesh, 2016). Vertical: a garment maker buys its own fabric mill.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>একীভূতকরণ</b> = <b>দুটি স্বাধীন কোম্পানির একত্রীকরণ</b>; সাধারণত <b>একটি বড় কোম্পানি</b> তৈরি হয় ও <b>একটি মূল কোম্পানির অস্তিত্ব থাকে না</b>। দুই ধরন:</p>\n<ul><li><b>অনুভূমিক</b> — <b>একই শিল্পের</b> কোম্পানির মধ্যে, প্রায়ই <b>প্রতিযোগী</b>; <b>কম প্রতিষ্ঠান</b> আছে এমন শিল্পে প্রচলিত।</li><li><b>উল্লম্ব</b> — <b>ক্রেতা-বিক্রেতা সম্পর্কের</b>, সরবরাহ শিকলের <b>ভিন্ন স্তরের</b> প্রতিষ্ঠানের মধ্যে; যুক্তি: একসাথে <b>বেশি দক্ষভাবে</b> চলে।</li></ul><p class=\"lab lab-E\"><b>উদাহরণ:</b> অনুভূমিক: দুটি মোবাইল অপারেটর একীভূত (রবি + এয়ারটেল বাংলাদেশ, ২০১৬)। উল্লম্ব: পোশাক প্রস্তুতকারক নিজের কাপড়ের মিল কেনে।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s52","k":"slide","t":"Acquisitions and reasons","tb":"অধিগ্রহণ ও কারণ","sl":[52,53],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 52–53 of 57 · স্লাইড ৫২–৫৩ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=52\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 52) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s52.webp\" alt=\"Slide 52 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s53.webp\" alt=\"Slide 53 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Defining Acquisitions An acquisition occurs when a company purchases the assets of another business (such as stock, property, plants, equipment) and usually permits the acquired company to continue operating as it did prior to the acquisition. Acquisition usually refers to a purchase of a smaller firm by a larger one. Sometimes a smaller firm will acquire management control of a larger and/or longer-established company and retain the name of the latter for the postacquisition combined entity.</p><p>Reasons for Mergers and Acquisitions •</p><p>• • • • • • •</p><p>Obtaining quality staff or additional skills, knowledge of your industry or sector, and other business intelligence Accessing funds or valuable assets for new development Your business is underperforming Accessing a wider customer base and increasing your market share Diversification of the products, services, and long-term prospects of your business Reducing your costs and overheads through shared marketing budgets, increased purchasing power, and lower costs Reducing competitions Organic growth</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> An <b>acquisition</b> = one company <b>buys the assets</b> (stock, property, plants, equipment) of another and usually lets it <b>keep operating</b>; usually a <b>larger firm buys a smaller one</b> (sometimes a smaller firm takes control and keeps the bigger name). <b>Reasons for M&A:</b> <b>skilled staff and knowledge</b>; <b>funds or valuable assets</b>; <b>underperformance</b>; <b>wider customer base and market share</b>; <b>diversification</b>; <b>cost reduction</b> (shared marketing, bigger buying power); <b>reducing competition</b>; <b>growth</b>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>অধিগ্রহণ</b> = এক কোম্পানি অন্যের <b>সম্পদ কেনে</b> (শেয়ার, সম্পত্তি, কারখানা, যন্ত্রপাতি) এবং সাধারণত তাকে <b>চলতে দেয়</b>; সাধারণত <b>বড় প্রতিষ্ঠান ছোটটিকে কেনে</b> (কখনো ছোট প্রতিষ্ঠান নিয়ন্ত্রণ নিয়ে বড়টির নাম রাখে)। <b>M&A-র কারণ:</b> <b>দক্ষ কর্মী ও জ্ঞান</b>; <b>তহবিল বা মূল্যবান সম্পদ</b>; <b>খারাপ কর্মক্ষমতা</b>; <b>বড় ক্রেতাভিত্তি ও বাজার অংশ</b>; <b>বৈচিত্র্য</b>; <b>খরচ কমানো</b> (যৌথ মার্কেটিং, বেশি ক্রয়ক্ষমতা); <b>প্রতিযোগিতা কমানো</b>; <b>প্রবৃদ্ধি</b>।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"s54","k":"slide","t":"Practice question 10, discussion, review","tb":"অনুশীলনী ১০, আলোচনা, পুনরালোচনা","sl":[54,55,56,57],"h":"<p class=\"slidebar\"><span>📑 Slides 54–57 of 57 · স্লাইড ৫৪–৫৭ / ৫৭</span><a href=\"slides/Introduction%20to%20Business%20%28BIBS%20101%29/Unit%2010%20and%2011%20-%20BusinessOwnership.pdf#page=54\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open original slide (PDF page 54) ↗</a></p><div class=\"slideimgs\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s54.webp\" alt=\"Slide 54 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s55.webp\" alt=\"Slide 55 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s56.webp\" alt=\"Slide 56 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"><img class=\"slideimg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"bibs/img/m07/s57.webp\" alt=\"Slide 57 of the original deck\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></div><div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<blockquote class=\"slidetext\"><span class=\"sl\">Slide text</span><p>Practice Question 10 What is the biggest benefit to businesses of horizontal mergers and acquisitions? A. Market valuation decreases B. Competition is reduced C. Customer feedback improves</p><p>D. Employee career paths lengthen</p><p>Class Discussion: Business Ownership As we have learned, businesses can have a variety of ownership structures based on the vision, size, liability. and control wanted by the organization. DIs it correct to assume that small businesses are set up as Sole Proprietorships and evolve into C Corporations as they grow? Match the company with its business structure: 1. American Airlines 2. IKEA 3. Intel 4. Exxon Mobile 5. Mars, Inc. 6. Apple 7. Dyson 8. Albertsons</p><p>Quick Review • What are the important factors in choosing an organizational type? • What are the advantages and disadvantages of sole proprietorships and partnerships? • What are the advantages and disadvantages of corporations? • What are the advantages and disadvantages of hybrid forms of business ownership? • What are the advantages and disadvantages of franchises? • What are the two types of mergers and acquisitions?</p></blockquote><p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>Tutor explains:</b> <b>Q10: B — competition is reduced</b> (the biggest benefit of horizontal M&A). Discussion: it is <b>not always true</b> that small firms start as sole proprietorships and end as C corporations — many stay small, choose LLCs, or are private (Mars, IKEA, Dyson are private; Apple, Intel, Exxon, American Airlines, Albertsons are public C corporations). Slide 57 lists the seven study questions.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<p class=\"lab lab-T\"><b>টিউটর বুঝিয়ে বলছেন:</b> <b>প্রশ্ন ১০: B — প্রতিযোগিতা কমে</b> (অনুভূমিক M&A-র বড় সুবিধা)। আলোচনা: ছোট প্রতিষ্ঠান একক মালিকানা থেকে শুরু করে C কর্পোরেশনে যায় — এটি <b>সবসময় সত্য নয়</b>; অনেকে ছোট থাকে, LLC নেয়, বা প্রাইভেট থাকে (মার্স, আইকিয়া, ডাইসন প্রাইভেট; অ্যাপল, ইন্টেল, এক্সন, আমেরিকান এয়ারলাইনস, অ্যালবার্টসনস পাবলিক C কর্পোরেশন)। স্লাইড ৫৭-এ সাতটি স্টাডি প্রশ্ন।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"c7-7","k":"check","t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","sl":[],"h":"","z":{"t":"Quick check","tb":"দ্রুত যাচাই","items":[{"q":"A merger between a manufacturer and its supplier is…","qbn":"উৎপাদক ও তার সরবরাহকারীর একীভূতকরণ…","ans":1,"opts":["horizontal · অনুভূমিক","vertical · উল্লম্ব","a franchise · ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ","a partnership · অংশীদারি"],"exp":"Firms at different levels of the supply chain: vertical.","expbn":"সরবরাহ শিকলের ভিন্ন স্তরের প্রতিষ্ঠান: উল্লম্ব।"},{"q":"The biggest benefit of horizontal mergers is…","qbn":"অনুভূমিক একীভূতকরণের বড় সুবিধা…","ans":1,"opts":["more competition · বেশি প্রতিযোগিতা","reduced competition · কম প্রতিযোগিতা","lower sales · কম বিক্রি","fewer customers · কম ক্রেতা"],"exp":"Merging competitors in the same industry reduces competition.","expbn":"একই শিল্পের প্রতিযোগীদের একীভূতকরণ প্রতিযোগিতা কমায়।"},{"q":"In an acquisition…","qbn":"অধিগ্রহণে…","ans":0,"opts":["a company purchases another's assets and usually lets it continue operating · এক কোম্পানি অন্যের সম্পদ কেনে ও সাধারণত চলতে দেয়","two firms vanish · দুটি প্রতিষ্ঠানই বিলুপ্ত","a firm is franchised · প্রতিষ্ঠান ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ হয়","a partner leaves · অংশীদার বেরিয়ে যায়"],"exp":"Acquisition = purchase of assets, typically by a larger firm of a smaller one.","expbn":"অধিগ্রহণ = সম্পদ কেনা, সাধারণত বড় প্রতিষ্ঠান ছোটটিকে।"}]}},{"id":"together","k":"together","t":"Comparison table","tb":"তুলনা টেবিল","sl":[],"h":"<div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Owners</th><th>Liability</th><th>Tax</th><th>Key point</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Sole proprietorship</td><td>1</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Personal</td><td>Simplest; hard to raise capital</td></tr>\n<tr><td>General partnership</td><td>2+</td><td>Unlimited, joint</td><td>Pass-through</td><td>Shared skills; disagreements</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Limited partnership/LLP</td><td>2+</td><td>Limited for some/all</td><td>Pass-through</td><td>Investor-friendly; protected from others' negligence</td></tr>\n<tr><td>C corporation</td><td>Shareholders</td><td>Limited</td><td>Double</td><td>Raise capital via stock; costly</td></tr>\n<tr><td>S corporation</td><td>Shareholders</td><td>Limited</td><td>Pass-through</td><td>No double tax; strict rules</td></tr>\n<tr><td>B corporation</td><td>Shareholders</td><td>Limited</td><td>As C or S</td><td>Public benefit + annual report</td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLC</td><td>Members</td><td>Limited</td><td>Pass-through</td><td>Flexible; self-employment tax</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Franchise</td><td>Franchisee</td><td>Varies</td><td>Per form</td><td>Brand + support vs fees and rules</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>রূপ</th><th>মালিক</th><th>দায়</th><th>কর</th><th>মূল কথা</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>একক মালিকানা</td><td>১</td><td>অসীম</td><td>ব্যক্তিগত</td><td>সবচেয়ে সহজ; মূলধন তোলা কঠিন</td></tr>\n<tr><td>সাধারণ অংশীদারি</td><td>২+</td><td>অসীম, যৌথ</td><td>পাস-থ্রু</td><td>ভাগ করা দক্ষতা; মতভেদ</td></tr>\n<tr><td>সীমিত অংশীদারি/LLP</td><td>২+</td><td>কিছু/সবার সীমিত</td><td>পাস-থ্রু</td><td>বিনিয়োগকারীবান্ধব; অন্যের অবহেলা থেকে সুরক্ষা</td></tr>\n<tr><td>C কর্পোরেশন</td><td>শেয়ারহোল্ডার</td><td>সীমিত</td><td>দ্বৈত</td><td>শেয়ারে মূলধন; ব্যয়বহুল</td></tr>\n<tr><td>S কর্পোরেশন</td><td>শেয়ারহোল্ডার</td><td>সীমিত</td><td>পাস-থ্রু</td><td>দ্বৈত কর নেই; কড়া নিয়ম</td></tr>\n<tr><td>B কর্পোরেশন</td><td>শেয়ারহোল্ডার</td><td>সীমিত</td><td>C বা S-এর মতো</td><td>জনকল্যাণ + বার্ষিক প্রতিবেদন</td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLC</td><td>সদস্য</td><td>সীমিত</td><td>পাস-থ্রু</td><td>নমনীয়; স্ব-কর্মসংস্থান কর</td></tr>\n<tr><td>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ</td><td>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজি</td><td>ভিন্ন</td><td>রূপ অনুযায়ী</td><td>ব্র্যান্ড + সহায়তা বনাম ফি ও নিয়ম</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div></div></div>"},{"id":"midterm","k":"midterm","t":"Exam answers 7.1–7.7","tb":"পরীক্ষার উত্তর ৭.১–৭.৭","sl":[],"h":"<div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<h3>7.1 Factors (slides 3–7)</h3>\n<p>Start-up cost; control vs responsibility; sharing profits; taxation; entrepreneurial ability; risk tolerance; financing; continuity and transferability. The best form depends on the opportunity and the owner's risk exposure.</p>\n<h3>7.2 Sole proprietorship (slides 8–12)</h3>\n<p>One owner, no distinction between owner and business. <b>Advantages:</b> easy/cheap to form, all profits, direct control, little regulation, no special tax, easy dissolution. <b>Disadvantages:</b> unlimited liability, hard to raise capital, limited expertise, time commitment, unstable life.</p>\n<h3>7.3 Partnerships (slides 13–21)</h3>\n<p>Two or more owners sharing money, skill, profits and losses. <b>General</b> (equal, unlimited liability) vs <b>limited/LLP</b> (limited liability and say). <b>Advantages:</b> easy to form, shared commitment, complementary skills. <b>Disadvantages:</b> joint and individual liability, disagreements, shared profits.</p>\n<h3>7.4 Corporations (slides 22–32)</h3>\n<p><b>C corp:</b> separate legal entity, limited liability, sells stock, but double taxation, cost and paperwork. <b>S corp:</b> IRS election, pass-through tax, strict operations, reasonable compensation. <b>B corp:</b> for-profit with public benefit and annual benefit report; mission protection and reputation vs reporting, fees and governance.</p>\n<h3>7.5 Hybrids (slides 33–40)</h3>\n<p><b>LLC:</b> limited liability + pass-through tax, flexible profit sharing; possible limited life and self-employment tax. <b>LLP:</b> partners protected from others' misconduct, single taxation, flexibility; unstable life, not recognized everywhere.</p>\n<h3>7.6 Franchises (slides 41–47)</h3>\n<p>Franchisee: lower risk, brand, support, autonomy vs cost, unequal partnership, strict rules. Franchisor: capital, royalties, economies of scale vs lack of control, trade-secret risk, brand dilution.</p>\n<h3>7.7 Mergers and acquisitions (slides 48–57)</h3>\n<p>Merger: two firms become one — <b>horizontal</b> (same industry; reduces competition) or <b>vertical</b> (buyer–seller, supply chain efficiency). Acquisition: purchase of another firm's assets. Reasons: skills, funds, market share, diversification, lower costs, less competition, growth.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<h3>৭.১ বিবেচ্য বিষয় (স্লাইড ৩–৭)</h3>\n<p>শুরুর খরচ; নিয়ন্ত্রণ বনাম দায়; লাভ ভাগ; কর; উদ্যোক্তা সক্ষমতা; ঝুঁকি সহনশীলতা; অর্থায়ন; ধারাবাহিকতা ও হস্তান্তর। সেরা রূপ নির্ভর করে সুযোগ ও মালিকের ঝুঁকির উপর।</p>\n<h3>৭.২ একক মালিকানা (স্লাইড ৮–১২)</h3>\n<p>একজন মালিক, মালিক ও ব্যবসায় পার্থক্য নেই। <b>সুবিধা:</b> গঠন সহজ/সস্তা, সব মুনাফা, সরাসরি নিয়ন্ত্রণ, কম নিয়ন্ত্রণ, বিশেষ কর নেই, বন্ধ সহজ। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> অসীম দায়, মূলধন তোলা কঠিন, সীমিত দক্ষতা, সময়ের চাপ, অস্থির জীবন।</p>\n<h3>৭.৩ অংশীদারি (স্লাইড ১৩–২১)</h3>\n<p>দুই বা ততোধিক মালিক টাকা, দক্ষতা, লাভ-ক্ষতি ভাগ করেন। <b>সাধারণ</b> (সমান, অসীম দায়) বনাম <b>সীমিত/LLP</b> (সীমিত দায় ও মতামত)। <b>সুবিধা:</b> গঠন সহজ, ভাগ করা দায়িত্ব, পরিপূরক দক্ষতা। <b>অসুবিধা:</b> যৌথ ও ব্যক্তিগত দায়, মতভেদ, মুনাফা ভাগ।</p>\n<h3>৭.৪ কর্পোরেশন (স্লাইড ২২–৩২)</h3>\n<p><b>C কর্পোরেশন:</b> আলাদা আইনি সত্তা, সীমিত দায়, শেয়ার বেচে মূলধন; কিন্তু দ্বৈত কর, খরচ ও কাগজপত্র। <b>S কর্পোরেশন:</b> IRS নির্বাচন, পাস-থ্রু কর, কড়া পরিচালনা, যুক্তিসঙ্গত পারিশ্রমিক। <b>B কর্পোরেশন:</b> জনকল্যাণসহ মুনাফাভিত্তিক ও বার্ষিক প্রতিবেদন; লক্ষ্য-সুরক্ষা ও সুনাম বনাম প্রতিবেদন, ফি ও পরিচালনার দায়।</p>\n<h3>৭.৫ হাইব্রিড (স্লাইড ৩৩–৪০)</h3>\n<p><b>LLC:</b> সীমিত দায় + পাস-থ্রু কর, নমনীয় মুনাফা ভাগ; সম্ভাব্য সীমিত জীবন ও স্ব-কর্মসংস্থান কর। <b>LLP:</b> অন্যের অন্যায় থেকে সুরক্ষা, একক কর, নমনীয়তা; অস্থির জীবন, সব রাজ্যে স্বীকৃত নয়।</p>\n<h3>৭.৬ ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ (স্লাইড ৪১–৪৭)</h3>\n<p>ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজি: কম ঝুঁকি, ব্র্যান্ড, সহায়তা, স্বায়ত্তশাসন বনাম খরচ, অসম অংশীদারি, কড়া নিয়ম। ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজর: মূলধন, রয়্যালটি, বৃহদায়তনের সুবিধা বনাম নিয়ন্ত্রণের অভাব, গোপনীয়তা ঝুঁকি, ব্র্যান্ড ক্ষয়।</p>\n<h3>৭.৭ একীভূতকরণ ও অধিগ্রহণ (স্লাইড ৪৮–৫৭)</h3>\n<p>একীভূতকরণ: দুই প্রতিষ্ঠান এক — <b>অনুভূমিক</b> (একই শিল্প; প্রতিযোগিতা কমে) বা <b>উল্লম্ব</b> (ক্রেতা-বিক্রেতা, সরবরাহ শিকলের দক্ষতা)। অধিগ্রহণ: অন্য প্রতিষ্ঠানের সম্পদ কেনা। কারণ: দক্ষতা, তহবিল, বাজার অংশ, বৈচিত্র্য, কম খরচ, কম প্রতিযোগিতা, প্রবৃদ্ধি।</p></div></div>"},{"id":"quiz","k":"quiz","t":"Module 7 quiz — 10 questions","tb":"মডিউল ৭ কুইজ — ১০টি প্রশ্ন","sl":[],"h":"","z":{"t":"Module 7 quiz — 10 questions","tb":"মডিউল ৭ কুইজ — ১০টি প্রশ্ন","items":[{"q":"Which form has no distinction between the owner and the business?","qbn":"কোন রূপে মালিক ও ব্যবসায় পার্থক্য নেই?","ans":2,"opts":["C corporation · C কর্পোরেশন","LLC · LLC","Sole proprietorship · একক মালিকানা","B corporation · B কর্পোরেশন"],"exp":"In a sole proprietorship the owner is the business.","expbn":"একক মালিকানায় মালিকই ব্যবসা।"},{"q":"Unlimited personal liability applies to…","qbn":"অসীম ব্যক্তিগত দায় প্রযোজ্য…","ans":2,"opts":["shareholders of a C corp · C কর্পোরেশনের শেয়ারহোল্ডারদের","LLC members · LLC সদস্যদের","sole proprietors and general partners · একক মালিক ও সাধারণ অংশীদারদের","B corp shareholders · B কর্পোরেশনের শেয়ারহোল্ডারদের"],"exp":"Sole proprietors and general partners are personally liable for business debts.","expbn":"একক মালিক ও সাধারণ অংশীদাররা ব্যবসার ঋণের জন্য ব্যক্তিগতভাবে দায়ী।"},{"q":"Partnerships typically…","qbn":"অংশীদারি সাধারণত…","ans":1,"opts":["pay corporate income tax · কর্পোরেট আয়কর দেয়","file an information return while partners pay tax on their share · তথ্য রিটার্ন দেয় আর অংশীদাররা নিজের ভাগে কর দেন","are taxed twice · দুইবার করযোগ্য","cannot have profits · মুনাফা রাখতে পারে না"],"exp":"Partnership income passes through to partners.","expbn":"অংশীদারির আয় অংশীদারদের কাছে যায়।"},{"q":"Which is NOT an advantage of partnerships?","qbn":"অংশীদারির সুবিধা নয় কোনটি?","ans":3,"opts":["Easy to form · গঠন সহজ","Complementary skills · পরিপূরক দক্ষতা","Shared financial commitment · ভাগ করা আর্থিক দায়িত্ব","Protection from all liability · সব দায় থেকে সুরক্ষা"],"exp":"General partners have unlimited, joint liability.","expbn":"সাধারণ অংশীদারদের অসীম, যৌথ দায়।"},{"q":"Double taxation is a drawback of…","qbn":"দ্বৈত কর অসুবিধা…","ans":2,"opts":["S corporations · S কর্পোরেশনের","LLCs · LLC-র","C corporations · C কর্পোরেশনের","LLPs · LLP-র"],"exp":"C-corp profits are taxed and then dividends again.","expbn":"C কর্পোরেশনের মুনাফায় কর, তারপর লভ্যাংশে আবার।"},{"q":"An S corporation is created through…","qbn":"S কর্পোরেশন তৈরি হয়…","ans":1,"opts":["a court order · আদালতের আদেশে","an IRS tax election · IRS কর নির্বাচনে","a franchise agreement · ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ চুক্তিতে","a merger · একীভূতকরণে"],"exp":"An eligible corporation elects S status to avoid double taxation.","expbn":"যোগ্য কর্পোরেশন দ্বৈত কর এড়াতে S মর্যাদা নেয়।"},{"q":"A B corporation differs from a C corporation mainly in…","qbn":"B কর্পোরেশন C কর্পোরেশন থেকে মূলত আলাদা…","ans":1,"opts":["taxation · করে","purpose, accountability and transparency · উদ্দেশ্য, জবাবদিহি ও স্বচ্ছতায়","number of owners · মালিকের সংখ্যায়","liability · দায়ে"],"exp":"B corps are taxed like C or S corps but must create public benefit and report.","expbn":"B কর্পোরেশন C বা S-এর মতো করযোগ্য কিন্তু জনকল্যাণ সৃষ্টি ও প্রতিবেদন করতে হয়।"},{"q":"Which hybrid gives corporate limited liability with partnership-style taxation and calls owners \"members\"?","qbn":"কোন হাইব্রিড কর্পোরেট সীমিত দায় ও অংশীদারির মতো কর দেয় এবং মালিকদের \"সদস্য\" বলে?","ans":2,"opts":["Franchise · ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ","S corporation · S কর্পোরেশন","LLC · LLC","Sole proprietorship · একক মালিকানা"],"exp":"That is the LLC.","expbn":"এটি LLC।"},{"q":"Which is a disadvantage for a franchisor?","qbn":"ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজরের অসুবিধা কোনটি?","ans":2,"opts":["Access to capital · মূলধনে প্রবেশাধিকার","Royalty income · রয়্যালটি আয়","Lack of control over quality and brand overexposure · মানের নিয়ন্ত্রণের অভাব ও ব্র্যান্ডের অতিরিক্ত প্রসার","Economies of scale · বৃহদায়তনের সুবিধা"],"exp":"Franchisors risk losing control and diluting the brand.","expbn":"ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজর নিয়ন্ত্রণ ও ব্র্যান্ড ক্ষয়ের ঝুঁকিতে।"},{"q":"A horizontal merger occurs between…","qbn":"অনুভূমিক একীভূতকরণ ঘটে…","ans":1,"opts":["a buyer and its supplier · ক্রেতা ও তার সরবরাহকারীর মধ্যে","companies in the same industry, often competitors · একই শিল্পের, প্রায়ই প্রতিযোগী কোম্পানির মধ্যে","a firm and a charity · প্রতিষ্ঠান ও দাতব্য সংস্থার মধ্যে","a franchisor and franchisee · ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজর ও ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজির মধ্যে"],"exp":"Horizontal = same industry; vertical = different supply-chain levels.","expbn":"অনুভূমিক = একই শিল্প; উল্লম্ব = সরবরাহ শিকলের ভিন্ন স্তর।"}]}},{"id":"summary","k":"summary","t":"Module 7 summary","tb":"মডিউল ৭ সারাংশ","sl":[],"h":"<div class=\"pair\">\n<div class=\"en\"><span class=\"tag\">English</span>\n<ul><li>8 factors to choose a form; sole proprietor (unlimited, simple), partnership (general vs limited), C/S/B corporations, LLC, LLP, franchise, merger vs acquisition.</li><li>Liability: unlimited (sole, general partner); limited (corporations, LLC, LLP). Tax: double (C), pass-through (S, LLC, partnership).</li><li>Merger: horizontal (competitors, less competition) vs vertical (supply chain).</li></ul>\n<p><b>Next:</b> Module 8 — Entrepreneurship.</p></div>\n<div class=\"bn-box\"><span class=\"tag\">বাংলা</span>\n<ul><li>রূপ বেছে নেওয়ার ৮ বিবেচ্য বিষয়; একক মালিক (অসীম, সহজ), অংশীদারি (সাধারণ বনাম সীমিত), C/S/B কর্পোরেশন, LLC, LLP, ফ্র্যাঞ্চাইজ, একীভূতকরণ বনাম অধিগ্রহণ।</li><li>দায়: অসীম (একক, সাধারণ অংশীদার); সীমিত (কর্পোরেশন, LLC, LLP)। কর: দ্বৈত (C), পাস-থ্রু (S, LLC, অংশীদারি)।</li><li>একীভূতকরণ: অনুভূমিক (প্রতিযোগী, কম প্রতিযোগিতা) বনাম উল্লম্ব (সরবরাহ শিকল)।</li></ul>\n<p><b>পরবর্তী:</b> মডিউল ৮ — উদ্যোক্তা।</p></div></div>"}]});
